## Draft attribution record
{
  "type": "attribution",
  "reported_by": "pr-code-review",
  "improves": "tdd",
  "improves_type": "skill",
  "cause": "general_best_practice",
  "cause_label": null,
  "problem": "_dedupe_column_names only tracks counts per original name and never checks whether a generated suffix already exists in the input list. Inputs like [\"Revenue\", \"Revenue 2\", \"Revenue\"] still produce two \"Revenue 2\" values, so df.rename raises DuplicateError.",
  "why_missed": "The parametrized test suite covered same-name-repeated patterns (e.g. [\"As Of Date\", \"As Of Date\", \"As Of Date\"]) and interleaved duplicates, but omitted the adversarial case where a generated suffix (\"Revenue 2\") already appears as a raw input name. That missing test case would have returned [\"Revenue\", \"Revenue 2\", \"Revenue 2\"] — a duplicate — and failed, driving an implementation fix.",
  "lesson": "For any function that generates uniqueness by appending a suffix, include a test case where the generated suffix already exists in the original input list (e.g. [base, \"base 2\", base]) to confirm the output contains no duplicates.",
  "fix": "Add a parametrized test case ([\"Revenue\", \"Revenue 2\", \"Revenue\"], expected=[\"Revenue\", \"Revenue 2\", \"Revenue 2 2\"]) or equivalent, and fix _dedupe_column_names to skip any candidate suffixed name that already exists in the full input set.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "source": "artifact",
      "ref": "app/firm_exports/dashboard.py",
      "quote": "    seen: dict[str, int] = {}\n    result: list[str] = []\n    for name in names:\n        if name in seen:\n            seen[name] += 1\n            result.append(f\"{name} {seen[name]}\")\n        else:\n            seen[name] = 1\n            result.append(name)\n    return result"
    },
    {
      "source": "artifact",
      "ref": "app/firm_exports/tests/test_portfolio_dashboard.py",
      "quote": "        (\n            [\"Revenue\", \"As Of Date\", \"Revenue\", \"As Of Date\", \"Revenue\"],\n            [\"Revenue\", \"As Of Date\", \"Revenue 2\", \"As Of Date 2\", \"Revenue 3\"],\n        ),"
    }
  ],
  "trace": {
    "pr": "https://github.com/Quaestor-Technologies/Quaestor-Web/pull/18191",
    "branch": "fix/portfolio-export-filter"
  },
  "confidence": "confirmed"
}

