## Draft attribution record
{
  "type": "attribution",
  "reported_by": "pr-revise",
  "improves": "build-runner",
  "improves_type": "agent",
  "cause": "context_lost_in_handoff",
  "cause_label": null,
  "problem": "The ORDERING_OPTIONS array in DataChecksInboxPanel.tsx maps 'Age: Newest first' to DataCheckItemsOrdering['-age'] and 'Age: Oldest first' to DataCheckItemsOrdering.age, inverting the intended sort labels. The backend (core.py:71) documents that ascending age (no dash) = smallest age = newest flagged_at, so '-age' returns oldest items, not newest.",
  "why_missed": "The build-runner's TDD cycle implemented the frontend sort label-to-value mapping without cross-referencing the backend's counterintuitive age-sort semantic. The API contract — that ascending 'age' field ordering yields newest items because age is measured from a reference point — was documented in core.py but not checked when writing the ORDERING_OPTIONS constants.",
  "lesson": "When implementing UI sort options that map human-readable labels to API ordering fields with counterintuitive direction semantics (e.g. ascending 'age' = newest, not oldest), explicitly verify the backend sort contract before writing the mapping. Fields named after duration/recency can have inverted semantics relative to their underlying timestamp.",
  "fix": "Add a checklist step to build-runner's task execution: when a task adds sort UI options for an API ordering field, require reading the backend sort implementation or OpenAPI docs to verify which direction key corresponds to which human direction before writing the label mapping.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "source": "artifact",
      "ref": "app/data_checks/core.py",
      "quote": "# Ascending age is the smallest age first, i.e. the newest `flagged_at`\n        # first, so the sort direction is inverted relative to the timestamp."
    },
    {
      "source": "artifact",
      "ref": "client/src/modules/data-checks/DataChecksInboxPanel.tsx",
      "quote": "{ value: DataCheckItemsOrdering['-age'], label: 'Age: Newest first' },\n  { value: DataCheckItemsOrdering.age, label: 'Age: Oldest first' },"
    }
  ],
  "trace": {
    "pr": "https://github.com/Quaestor-Technologies/Quaestor-Web/pull/18776",
    "branch": "key-2120-data-checks-ui-build-the-resolved-inbox-list"
  },
  "confidence": "candidate"
}

