{
  "type": "attribution",
  "reported_by": "pr-code-review",
  "improves": "run-tasks",
  "improves_type": "skill",
  "cause": "data_contract_gap",
  "cause_label": null,
  "problem": "PR added MULTI_SELECT inputUnit support to EditableTable.tsx and EditableMetrics.tsx but left both mutation paths unguarded: EditableMetrics.tsx L127 applies value.replace(/,/g, '') without checking for MULTI_SELECT, corrupting JSON array strings like '[\"optionA\",\"optionB\"]' into '[\"optionA\"\"optionB\"]'. useMetricsTableCrud/index.tsx L118 does the same with no inputUnit guard at all. Full deselection passes null, crashing both paths with TypeError on .replace().",
  "why_missed": "The mutation function updateMyData in EditableMetrics.tsx had an implicit assumption that all non-STRING values are numeric or scalar and safe to strip commas. This assumption was not expressed as a type constraint. The PR updated the rendering path (EditableTable.tsx) and column mapping (EditableMetrics.tsx) to propagate MULTI_SELECT as an inputUnit, but did not audit how the mutation consumer processes that value before posting to the API.",
  "lesson": "When a PR introduces a new inputUnit type that serializes differently from all existing types (JSON array vs. scalar), audit every downstream path that processes the raw value — especially mutation functions with format-stripping transforms — and add a type-specific guard before merging.",
  "fix": "In EditableMetrics.tsx L127, extend the guard to skip .replace for MULTI_SELECT: `metricCategory === Category.CUSTOM && (inputUnit === ValueType.STRING || inputUnit === ValueType.MULTI_SELECT) ? value : value?.replace(/,/g, '')`. In useMetricsTableCrud/index.tsx L118, apply the same pattern. Also guard all callers against null before calling .replace().",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "source": "artifact",
      "ref": "clients/web/src/pages/portfolio-company/EditableMetrics.tsx",
      "quote": "const formattedValue =\n      metricCategory === Category.CUSTOM && inputUnit === ValueType.STRING ? value : value.replace(/,/g, '')"
    },
    {
      "source": "artifact",
      "ref": "clients/web/src/pages/metrics-repository/components/DatumCategorySections/hooks/useMetricsTableCrud/index.tsx",
      "quote": "body: { value: value.replace(/,/g, '') || null, currency }"
    }
  ],
  "trace": {
    "pr": "https://github.com/Quaestor-Technologies/Quaestor-Web/pull/19500",
    "branch": "feat/KEY-2347-4-14-multi-select-fe-ir-response-inp"
  },
  "confidence": "candidate"
}

