  "problem": "parseDate in date-utils.ts has no year-range guard. date-fns parse() with format token yyyy is width-lenient (matches 1–4 digits), so '12/25/25' via MM/dd/yyyy yields year 0025. A manual refactor commit (54173d1479) moved date-utils.ts to a new location and rewrote it, dropping MIN_DATE, MAX_DATE, and validateDateRange that had been correctly implemented in T-0001 (commit 6d787620be). Without a minDate guard, a year-25 Date reaches the form.",
  "why_missed": "The initial T-0001 implementation correctly carried forward the legacy minDate/maxDate constraints. A subsequent manual refactor (commit 54173d1479, 'refactor: move date-utils.ts alongside DateInput') rewrote the file and dropped all three safety artifacts (MIN_DATE, MAX_DATE, validateDateRange) without recognizing that (a) date-fns yyyy token is width-lenient and (b) dropping the narrow MM/dd/yy format does not prevent 2-digit years from silently resolving via the wider MM/dd/yyyy format. This commit had no T-XXXX task ID, indicating it was user-initiated outside the skill pipeline.",
  "lesson": "When rewriting or moving a date-parsing utility, explicitly audit which safety constraints existed in the original (min/max date guards, year-range validators) and carry them forward. If dropping a narrow format (e.g. MM/dd/yy) to avoid 2-digit year ambiguity, verify that remaining wide formats (yyyy) do not silently absorb those inputs via parser width-leniency. Either restore a validateDateRange guard or add a post-parse year sanity check (e.g. getFullYear() >= 1900).",
