  "lesson": "When a hook parameter is added for caller integration, at least one production callsite must pass it before the PR is merged. Additionally, when a block reads a key under one casing convention and writes it under another, the test must either use real Formik state or an explicit contract comment must document the difference — mocking getIn at the path level can silently mask key-name bugs.",
